{
 "time": "2026-10-18-083606Z",
 "what": "eager tree decode plus walk plus destruction of one whole document, per document. B, B2 = cbor::decode of 50e0d19 (B built twice: noise floor). W1 = one-file test decoder: compact 24-byte node (type, info, union of u64/double/string_view/span<byte>/span<node>/tag{number,node*}) in one std::pmr::monotonic_buffer_resource on the stack, recursive, error code return and node out-parameter. W2 = W1 decoded iteratively with an explicit std::array stack bounded by the depth limit. W3 = W1 with scalar children decoded inline in the container loop and strings copied with an inline bump over 8 KiB chunks of the resource. MPC = msgpack-cxx v1 unpack.hpp context/unpack_stack/push_aggregate/push_item copied, msgpack::zone and msgpack::object kept, msgpack format bytes replaced by cbor heads::decoder and the checks of cbor::decode (CBOR input). MP = msgpack::unpack (resolves to the v2 parse_helper/create_object_visitor code) and a walk, input: the one msgpack buffer, the same one in every iteration (as in the earlier runs). MPI = MP on the rotating copies of the input, as the CBOR arms read. All CBOR arms check: pending items against bytes left, nesting depth, simple value, string length against bytes left. W1, W2, W3, MPC do not convert bignums and do not decode tag 24; no document needs it (equal sums).",
